# Button Navigation

Do not nest `<Link>` inside `<Button>` (e.g. `render={<Link to="..." />}`). This causes console warnings and invalid DOM nesting.

Use `useNavigate()` from `@tanstack/react-router` and call `navigate()` from an `onClick` handler or a separate function.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
import { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router';

<Button variant="outline" render={<Link to="/" />}>
  Stop
</Button>

// ✅ GOOD — inline onClick
import { useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router';

const navigate = useNavigate();

<Button
  variant="outline"
  onClick={() => navigate({ to: '/player', search: { categoryId } })}
>
  Play
</Button>

// ✅ GOOD — separate handler
function navigateToTopic() {
  navigate({
    to: '/categories/$categoryId/topics/$topicId',
    params: { categoryId, topicId },
  });
}

<Button type="button" variant="outline" onClick={handleCancel}>
  Cancel
</Button>
```

- Use `<Link>` for plain text or icon links that are not rendered as `<Button>`.
- Set `type="button"` when the button is inside a `<form>` and should not submit.
